   by ultrashort pulses},
Journal = {JOURNAL OF THE OPTICAL SOCIETY OF AMERICA B-OPTICAL PHYSICS},
Year = {1998},
Volume = {15},
Number = {7},
Pages = {1918-1922},
Month = {JUL},
Abstract = {We present results of experiments to determine the spectral and angular
   dependence of nonlinear scattering by water microdroplets of radii
   ranging from 1 to 32 mu m illuminated by ultrashort laser pulses. The
   main process observed is third-harmonic generation (THG). Moreover, in
   contrast with linear Mie scattering, the angular pattern of the THG is
   remarkably stable over the size range 8-32 mu m. (C) 1998 Optical
   Society of America.},
