   KONSTANZ, FED REP GER, SEP 10-14, 1990},
Abstract = {Metal clusters are generated via laser vaporization technique, but in
   contrast to common designs metal wires are used as target materials. 
   This allowed to simplify the construction of the source dramatically,
   because buffer gas leakage and hole drilling by the laser beam could
   easily be prevented.  The source produces neutral clusters as well as
   charged clusters (negative and positive).  Time-of-flight mass
   spectrometry was used to characterize these three different cluster
   distributions for two target materials:  silver and gold.},
